{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1021", "sample_idx": 8, "model_name": "qwen/qwen3-next-80b-a3b-instruct", "content": "PARAGRAPH 1  \nTHE SENTENCE \"IF THE LAW IS BAD, YOU SHOULD NOT FOLLOW IT\" IS OVERSIMPLIFIED TO THE POINT OF DANGEROUSNESS. IT IMPLIES A CLEAR, OBJECTIVE MEASURE OF WHAT CONSTITUTES A “BAD” LAW, WHEN IN REALITY, SUCH JUDGMENTS ARE HIGHLY SUBJECTIVE, CULTURALLY CONTEXTUAL, AND OFTEN INFLUENCED BY POWER STRUCTURES. IF EVERY INDIVIDUAL DECIDES FOR THEMSELVES WHEN TO DISREGARD THE LAW BASED ON PERSONAL MORALITY, THE FOUNDATION OF CIVIL ORDER BEGINS TO CRUMBLE. HISTORY SHOWS THAT UNCHECKED CIVIL DISOBEDIENCE CAN LEAD TO CHAOS, NOT JUSTICE—AS SEEING “BAD LAWS” AS A JUSTIFICATION FOR NONCOMPLIANCE IGNORES THE PROCEDURAL MECHANISMS FOR CHANGE, SUCH AS LEGISLATION, JUDICIAL REVIEW, AND CIVIC ENGAGEMENT.\n\nPARAGRAPH 2  \nFURTHERMORE, THE SENTENCE’S ABSOLUTIST TONE UNDERMINES THE COMPLEX RELATIONSHIP BETWEEN LAW AND MORALITY. WHILE THERE ARE HISTORICAL EXAMPLES WHERE DISOBEDIENCE TO UNJUST LAWS WAS MORALLY JUSTIFIED—SUCH AS THE CIVIL RIGHTS MOVEMENT—THESE WERE OFTEN PART OF ORGANIZED, NONVIOLENT MOVEMENTS THAT ACCEPTED THE CONSEQUENCES OF THEIR ACTIONS. THE SENTENCE, BY CONTRAST, SUGGESTS A PRIVILEGED INDIVIDUALISM THAT CAN BE EXPLOITED BY THOSE SEEKING TO JUSTIFY CRIMINAL BEHAVIOR OR ANARCHY. A HEALTHY SOCIETY DOES NOT REJECT LAW BASED ON PERSONAL OPINION BUT WORKS TO IMPROVE IT THROUGH DEMOCRATIC MEANS. THE SENTENCE, THEREFORE, IS NOT JUST INCOMPLETE—IT IS POTENTIALLY SUBVERSIVE TO THE RULE OF LAW ITSELF.", "logprobs": [{"token": "PAR", "logprob": -2.3841855067985307e-07}, {"token": "AGR", "logprob": -2.8371408916427754e-05}, {"token": "APH", "logprob": -8.344646857949556e-07}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -2.4318398573086597e-05}, {"token": "1", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "  \n", "logprob": -0.0019357530400156975}, {"token": "THE", "logprob": -0.012586444616317749}, {"token": " SENT", "logprob": -0.030008774250745773}, {"token": "ENCE", "logprob": -3.4212